dpdk: cap the frame size at the MTU limit the PMD reports

dpdk_device_setup sizes the port from dev_info.max_rx_pktlen only. Some
PMDs report a fixed value there and the real limit in max_mtu: virtio
always gives 9728, while max_mtu comes from the host's host_mtu, which
Proxmox VE sets to the bridge MTU (1500 by default). VPP then asks for
an MTU of 8996 (2022 with no-multi-seg), rte_eth_dev_configure refuses
it, every queue setup fails with -EINVAL and the port stays in
pmd-init-fail.

Also cap max_supported_frame_size at max_mtu plus the driver frame
overhead when the PMD reports a max_mtu. PMDs that leave max_mtu at
UINT16_MAX are not affected, and for PMDs whose two values agree the
cap is not lower than max_rx_pktlen.

--- a/src/plugins/dpdk/device/common.c
+++ b/src/plugins/dpdk/device/common.c
@@ -227,6 +227,15 @@
   else
     xd->max_supported_frame_size = dev_info.max_rx_pktlen;
 
+  /* Some PMDs report a fixed max_rx_pktlen and the real limit in max_mtu.
+     virtio gives 9728 while the host caps the MTU with host_mtu (1500 on
+     Proxmox VE); a larger MTU then fails rte_eth_dev_configure and the
+     port never comes up. */
+  if (dev_info.max_mtu != UINT16_MAX)
+    xd->max_supported_frame_size =
+      clib_min (xd->max_supported_frame_size,
+		(u32) dev_info.max_mtu + xd->driver_frame_overhead);
+
   max_frame_size = clib_min (xd->max_supported_frame_size,
 			     ethernet_main.default_mtu + hi->frame_overhead);
 
